 ## Background
-MAtCha was introduced as a heuristic-based approach for sparse view novel view synthesis (NVS) [S2, unofficial]. It is part of the broader family of methods that use MLPs for geometry and color effects, distinct from FFN-based approaches [S2, unofficial]. The method is cited in surveys covering the transition from volume rendering to 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1][S2, unofficial].
+MAtCha was introduced as part of the evolution from volume rendering to 3D Gaussian Splatting techniques for avatar generation [S1][S2, unofficial]. It is categorized as a heuristic-based sparse view Novel View Synthesis (NVS) method [S1][S2, unofficial]. The method addresses the challenge of reconstructing high-quality geometry when input views are sparse and have limited overlap, a common difficulty in real-world capture scenarios [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
